<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Nusa Tenggara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West Nusa Tenggara is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> made up of the islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombok">Lombok</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a>, with its capital at Mataram on Lombok. Formed in 1958, it includes the lands of the former sultanates of Sumbawa, Dompu and Bima. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-tambora">Mount Tambora</a>, whose eruption in 1815 was the largest in recorded history, stands on Sumbawa, and Mount Rinjani on Lombok.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-nusa-tenggara.jpg" alt="West Nusa Tenggara" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Nusa_Tenggara_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
